    "review": "The run ended blocked, not dead: the last accepted action left the Mage at 74/75 HP with purification active. The initiating failure was a newly visible necromancer occupying the fixed gas-room return waypoint 481 (decision 4220, lines 12434–12437). The public map at that decision offered a dry, visible alternative through 482, 523 and 522 to the original bank 563. Its four moves fit seven observed immunity turns with the existing two-turn margin. Instead, recovery attacked without moving; the next observation added a skeleton at 482, excluding that later escape. A focused correction now permits a duration-checked, freshly observed dry detour to the same bank, only for an occupied gas-return waypoint and with at most one extra move. It preserves hazard exclusions, protection checks, reward identity and collection requirements. The reduced regression reconstructs the journey from public route selections, not recorded runtime memory; whole-policy reconstruction was not performed. Original source fails the expected assertion; the candidate passes all three new tests and the full suite of 2,078 tests, with four skips. This establishes an admitted alternative selection, not successful escape, puzzle completion or improved survival. No patch content is embedded here; changed policy and the new regression are left for the trusted adapter.",
    "learnings": "A protected return should not insist on an occupied waypoint when a freshly observed dry detour reaches the same bank within the actual immunity budget. Recheck each subsequent observation; never reuse the earlier empty destination after a new enemy appears, invent collection, or replace planner exhaustion with waiting."
